.TH ELKS_COMPAT 4 "March 2026" "Substrate" "Kernel Interfaces"
.SH NAME
elks_compat \- compatibility notes for ELKS programs on Substrate
.SH DESCRIPTION
This document records the current ELKS compatibility envelope in Substrate.
It describes the implemented ELKS personality, the major known gaps, and the
places where ELKS behavior is translated rather than reproduced natively.
.SH COMPATIBLE AREAS
The following areas are implemented in the current tree:
.IP \(bu 2
ELKS Minix-style 16-bit
.B a.out
recognition
.IP \(bu
private per-process LDT allocation, duplication on
.BR fork (2),
replacement on
.BR execve (2),
and cleanup on exit/reap
.IP \(bu
16-bit startup stack image for
.B argc
,
.B argv
,
and
.B envp
.IP \(bu
ELKS
.BR INT\ 0x80
syscall dispatch for the active translated syscall table
.IP \(bu
ELKS callback-style signal delivery
.IP \(bu
smoke-tested hello, sleep/signal, file-I/O, and fork/wait execution
.SH KNOWN LIMITATIONS
.IP \(bu 2
Only the active translated ELKS syscall set is supported. Unimplemented slots
return
.BR ENOSYS .
.IP \(bu
ELKS file I/O has been smoke-tested on ext2 root. Other filesystems have not
been validated as an ELKS compatibility target.
.IP \(bu
ELKS core handling currently captures in-kernel crash state through the generic
core-dump policy hook; persistent core-file emission is not yet implemented.
.IP \(bu
The LDT bounds-violation validation item is not complete. Current bounds-fault
testing still exposes an unresolved fault-handling issue.
.IP \(bu
No general claim is made yet for running an entire upstream ELKS userland.
.SH INCOMPATIBILITIES
.TP
.B INT 0x20
Substrate does not support Minix-86 syscall entry for ELKS processes.
An ELKS process executing
.B INT 0x20
is treated as an incompatibility trap and rejected.
.TP
.B Native signal ABI
ELKS does not observe the native i386 or Linux i386 signal frame layout.
Signal delivery uses the ELKS-specific callback contract instead.
.TP
.B Flat 32-bit process ABI
ELKS does not use the native 32-bit ELF process-entry or pointer model.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR personality_elks (7),
.BR elks_aout (4)
